chapters.original_cn:
不尚贤,使民不争;
不贵难得之货,使民不为盗;
不见可欲,使民心不乱。
是以圣人之治,
虚其心,实其腹;
弱其志,强其骨。
常使民无知无欲,
使夫智者不敢为也。
为无为,则无不治。

持而盈之,不如其已;
揣而锐之,不可长保。
金玉满堂,莫之能守;
富贵而骄,自遗其咎。
功成身退,天之道也。

古之善为士者,微妙玄通,深不可识。
夫唯不可识,故强为之容:
豫兮,若冬涉川;
犹兮,若畏四邻;
俨兮,其若客;
涣兮,若冰之将释;
敦兮,其若朴;
旷兮,其若谷;
混兮,其若浊。
孰能浊以止?静之徐清。
孰能安以久?动之徐生。
保此道者不欲盈。
夫唯不盈,故能蔽不新成。

太上,不知有之;
其次,亲而誉之;
其次,畏之;
其次,侮之。
信不足焉,有不信焉。
悠兮,其贵言。
功成事遂,百姓皆谓我自然。

绝圣弃智,民利百倍;
绝仁弃义,民复孝慈;
绝巧弃利,盗贼无有。
此三者,以为文不足,故令有所属:
见素抱朴,少私寡欲,绝学无忧。

chapters.original_en:
Bent, then whole;
crooked, then straight;
hollow, then full;
worn, then new;
few, then gain;
many, then confused.
Therefore the sage holds to the one, and becomes the model of the world.
Does not show self, therefore bright;
does not deem self right, therefore manifest;
does not boast self, therefore meritorious;
does not pride self, therefore enduring.
Only because does not contend, no one under heaven can contend with him.
The ancients' saying "bent then whole" — is it empty words?
Truly whole, return to it.

Tiptoeing, one does not stand;
striding, one does not walk.
Those who show self are not bright;
those who deem self right are not manifest;
those who boast self are not meritorious;
those who pride self are not enduring.
In the Dao, these are called:
surplus food, superfluous conduct.
Things may dislike them,
therefore those who have Dao do not dwell in them.

Good traveling leaves no tracks;
good speaking leaves no flaws to be picked;
good counting needs no counting rods;
good closing needs no bolt yet cannot be opened;
good tying needs no rope yet cannot be untied.
Therefore the sage always saves people, therefore no one is abandoned;
always saves things, therefore nothing is abandoned.
This is called following brightness.
Therefore good people are the teachers of those who are not good;
those who are not good are the resources of good people.
Do not value the teacher, do not love the resource,
though intelligent, is greatly confused.
This is called subtle essence.

Those who know others are intelligent;
those who know themselves are bright.
Those who overcome others are strong;
those who overcome themselves are powerful.
Those who know contentment are rich;
those who persist are willful.
Those who do not lose their place endure;
those who die but do not perish are long-lived.

chapters.original_cn:
将欲歙之, 必固张之;
将欲弱之, 必固强之;
将欲废之, 必固兴之;
将欲夺之, 必固与之。
是谓微明。
柔弱胜刚强。
鱼不可脱于渊, 国之利器不可以示人。

知者不言,
言者不知。
塞其兑,闭其门;
挫其锐,解其纷;
和其光,同其尘,
是谓玄同。
故不可得而亲,
不可得而疏;
不可得而利,
不可得而害;
不可得而贵,
不可得而贱,
故为天下贵。

其安易持,其未兆易谋;
其脆易泮,其微易散。
为之于未有,治之于未乱。
合抱之木,生于毫末;
九层之台,起于累土;
千里之行,始于足下。
民之从事,常于几成而败之。
慎终如始,则无败事。

